9	+      # **What a failure leaves behind.** Two failures in this suite were lost
10	+      # last week with nothing kept about either: a line of output, and no
11	+      # screen, network or console to look at afterwards. Playwright keeps a
12	+      # trace for every test that fails and throws away the rest
13	+      # (`playwright.config.ts`), so there is something here exactly when there
14	+      # is a failure to read — open it with `npx playwright show-trace`. It runs
15	+      # even though the step above failed, which is the only time it has
16	+      # anything to do.
17	+      - name: Keep what the failures left behind
18	+        if: failure()
19	+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
20	+        with:
21	+          name: e2e-traces
